        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Unit members are compensated for their teaching, scholarship, creative activity and service to the public, their institution, and their profession. The University of Alaska's compensation program is designed to support the teaching, research, and service mission of the University through the recruitment and retention of outstanding unit members. This is to be accomplished by maintaining a competitive compensation plan and salary structure consistent with the University's needs and resources.",
            "block_bbox": [
                245,
